{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019884-help-with-new-legacy-the-agers","id":1019884,"title":"Help with new Legacy: The Agers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-20T11:53:54-08:00","id":1019884,"title":"Help with new Legacy: The Agers","content":"I\u2019m trying to formalize a Legacy I\u2019ve had in unfinished for years.<br /> They are a Moros Legacy. They are of the belief that the mere fact that an event gives rise to a ghost is reason to expect a given area/item to be of importance to long term Fate. They will always be on the lookout for hauntings. Upon finding them, especially if they can see specific traces of destiny (but sometimes even if not) they will try to acquire the area containing the anchor. They will then maintain and explore the area, looking for any secrets it may contain, and protecting it from needless destruction. While they concentrate on their specific houses/items/territories, they are of the belief that this is also helpful long term to surrounding communities / states, etc.. I've got a good feel for requirments, yantras, etc, but not attainments.<br /> <br /> They were conceived as having Fate as their additional Arcanum:<br /> <br /> Attainments:<br /> 1<sup>st</sup> attainment: Marks left that Matter: Fate 1, Death 1 \u2013 basically interconnections, but only detecting links to ghosts. The woman who lives in a haunted house, or the teacup that has sat in a kitchen where a ghost lurks for years would show links to the mage, which he can then follow up. I would like this to be constant, but I\u2019m not sure that is a thing with 2e rules, so possibly just use the free reach for instant effect.<br /> <br /> And that was it. I could not come up with any other Fate effects that I felt worked as attainments. So then I considered retooling them as Space based \u2013 their basic practices being the same, but concentrating on the holding of territory to protect and study it without the Fate connections. They would have to formally claim territory somehow to make it theirs, but the methods could vary (legally buying it, having the rights to an area awarded by a Consilium, trading rights to an area from a werewolf pack \u2013 all these work). I do not like this theme nearly as much, but was able to do better with the attainments:<br /> <br /> 1<sup>st</sup> Attainment: Marks left that Matter: Space 1, Death 1 \u2013 The same, but with Correspondence instead of Interconnections. To work the way I want it to, two reaches would be needed \u2013 instant casting, and the reach to allow a mage to actually follow a thread. I think this may be allowable since two arcana are involved, and the effect is limited compared to the full spell. I would also actually like to be constant, if that is a reasonable option.<br /> <br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> Attainment: Always Watching: Space 2 \u2013 Scrying on anywhere in his territory, provided the mage has marked the area observed with a personal rune to act as a sympathetic yantra.<br /> Alternate: Death 1 \u2013 I wanted the mage at this point to pretty much have constant \u201cspeak with the dead\u201d going on, possibly with a downside of distraction if there are too many ghosts around. Turning this off would require specifically casting the equivalent of a reverse \u201cspeak with the dead\u201d spell. If being constant isn\u2019t workable, I would have to go with something totally different.<br /> <br /> 3<sup>rd</sup> Attainment: Free Passage: Space 3 \u2013 Co- Location anywhere within the mages territories, proved that A.) each point can be seen as some sort of portal (door, cave mouth, two trees standing next to each other just so), and B.) the location has also been marked with a rune. Technically this requires 2 reaches (one for instant, one to create the portal effect described under +1 reach for the spell). I hope to get away with this due to the fact that the portal is always transitory (it is not possible to make it last longer than it takes the mage to pass through with anything/one he carries or leads by the hand) and the other requirements mean this is less versatile than the spell as written, not more so.<br /> <br /> Alternate: Death 3 \u2013 as above, but it\u2019s a Ghost Gate.<br /> <br /> That's all I've got for now. The first three attainments are the most important, Since characters with Gnosis over 4 are very rare in our games (even more so for PC's).<br /> I'm looking for any suggestions - either to salvage this with good Fate attainments that fit for legacy, or suggestions / criticisms on the correctness or playability of what I already have (and 4 and 5 attainments would be nice).<br /> <br /> Thanks for any feedback.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:10:16-08:00","id":1019896,"title":"","content":"Death 2 attainment is unnecessary since at that point you can just use the Death arcana utility attainment instead. The only thing the spell would be good for is communicating with ghosts that use an unfamiliar language. Even the anchor sensing function is already covered by just activating Active Mage Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:22:42-08:00","id":1019904,"title":"","content":"By the way I can see two angles for making the Fate thing work, they can empower ghosts to fulfill the destiny they didn't get to when they were alive, or they could steal those unfinished destinies in order to empower themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}